#: src/development/linux.md:53
msgid "**_Note_**: If you encounter linker errors similar to the following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:57 src/development/linux.md:59
msgid "':\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:61
msgid "'\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:66
msgid "\"remote_server\""
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:69
msgid ""
"**Cause**: This is caused by known bugs in aws-lc-rs (no GCC >= 14 support): "
"[FIPS fails to build with GCC >= 14](https://github.com/aws/aws-lc-rs/"
"issues/569) & [GCC-14 - build failure for FIPS module](https://github.com/"
"aws/aws-lc/issues/2010)"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:73
msgid ""
"You can refer to [linux: Linker error for remote_server when using script/"
"install-linux](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/24880) for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:75
msgid ""
"**Workaround**: Set the remote server target to `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` "
"like so `export REMOTE_SERVER_TARGET=x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu; script/"
"install-linux`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:78
msgid "Wayland & X11"
msgstr "Wayland 和 X11"

#: src/development/linux.md:80
msgid ""
"Zed supports both X11 and Wayland. By default, we pick whichever we can find "
"at runtime. If you're on Wayland and want to run in X11 mode, use the "
"environment variable `WAYLAND_DISPLAY=''`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:82
msgid "Notes for packaging Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:84
msgid "This section is for distribution maintainers packaging Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:86
msgid "Technical requirements"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:88
msgid "Zed has two main binaries:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:90
msgid ""
"You will need to build `crates/cli` and make its binary available in `$PATH` "
"with the name `zed`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:91
msgid ""
"You will need to build `crates/zed` and put it at `$PATH/to/cli/../../"
"libexec/zed-editor`. For example, if you are going to put the cli at `~/."
"local/bin/zed` put zed at `~/.local/libexec/zed-editor`. As some linux "
"distributions (notably Arch) discourage the use of `libexec`, you can also "
"put this binary at `$PATH/to/cli/../../lib/zed/zed-editor` (e.g. `~/.local/"
"lib/zed/zed-editor`) instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:92
msgid ""
"If you are going to provide a `.desktop` file you can find a template in "
"`crates/zed/resources/zed.desktop.in`, and use `envsubst` to populate it "
"with the values required. This file should also be renamed to `$APP_ID."
"desktop` so that the file [follows the FreeDesktop standards](https://github."
"com/zed-industries/zed/issues/12707#issuecomment-2168742761). You should "
"also make this desktop file executable (`chmod 755`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:93
msgid ""
"You will need to ensure that the necessary libraries are installed. You can "
"get the current list by [inspecting the built binary](https://github.com/zed-"
"industries/zed/blob/935cf542aebf55122ce6ed1c91d0fe8711970c82/script/bundle-"
"linux#L65-L67) on your system."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:94
msgid ""
"For an example of a complete build script, see [script/bundle-linux](https://"
"github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/935cf542aebf55122ce6ed1c91d0fe8711970c82/"
"script/bundle-linux)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:95
msgid ""
"You can disable Zed's auto updates and provide instructions for users who "
"try to update Zed manually by building (or running) Zed with the environment "
"variable `ZED_UPDATE_EXPLANATION`. For example: "
"`ZED_UPDATE_EXPLANATION=\"Please use flatpak to update zed.\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:96
msgid ""
"Make sure to update the contents of the `crates/zed/RELEASE_CHANNEL` file to "
"'nightly', 'preview', or 'stable', with no newline. This will cause Zed to "
"use the credentials manager to remember a user's login."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:98
msgid "Other things to note"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:100
msgid ""
"Zed moves quickly, and distribution maintainers often have different "
"constraints and priorities. The points below describe current trade-offs:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:102
msgid ""
"Zed is a fast-moving project. We typically publish 2-3 builds per week to "
"address reported issues and ship larger changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:103
msgid ""
"There are a couple of other `zed` binaries that may be present on Linux "
"systems ([1](https://openzfs.github.io/openzfs-docs/man/v2.2/8/zed.8.html), "
"[2](https://zed.brimdata.io/docs/commands/zed)). If you want to rename our "
"CLI binary because of these issues, we suggest `zedit`, `zeditor`, or `zed-"
"cli`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:104
msgid ""
"Zed automatically installs versions of common developer tools, similar to "
"rustup/rbenv/pyenv. This behavior is discussed [here](https://github.com/zed-"
"industries/zed/issues/12589)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:105
msgid ""
"Users can install extensions locally and from [zed-industries/extensions]"
"(https://github.com/zed-industries/extensions). Extensions may install "
"additional tools such as language servers. Planned safety improvements are "
"tracked [here](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/12358)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:106
msgid ""
"Zed connects to several online services by default (AI, telemetry, "
"collaboration). AI and our telemetry can be disabled by your users with "
"their zed settings or by patching our [default settings file](https://github."
"com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/assets/settings/default.json)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:107
msgid ""
"Because of the points above, Zed currently does not work well with "
"sandboxes. See [this discussion](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/"
"pull/12006#issuecomment-2130421220)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:109
msgid "Flatpak"
msgstr "Flatpak"

#: src/development/linux.md:111
msgid ""
"Zed's current Flatpak integration exits the sandbox on startup. Workflows "
"that rely on Flatpak's sandboxing may not work as expected."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:113
msgid "To build & install the Flatpak package locally follow the steps below:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:115
msgid ""
"Install Flatpak for your distribution as outlined [here](https://flathub.org/"
"setup)."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:116
msgid ""
"Run the `script/flatpak/deps` script to install the required dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:117
msgid "Run `script/flatpak/bundle-flatpak`."
msgstr "執行 `script/flatpak/bundle-flatpak`。"

#: src/development/linux.md:118
msgid ""
"Now the package has been installed and has a bundle available at `target/"
"release/{app-id}.flatpak`."
msgstr ""

