msgid ""
"[`heaptrack`](https://github.com/KDE/heaptrack) is quite useful for "
"diagnosing memory leaks. To install it:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:129
msgid "Then, to build and run Zed with the profiler attached:"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:135
msgid ""
"When this zed instance is exited, terminal output will include a command to "
"run `heaptrack_interpret` to convert the `*.raw.zst` profile to a `*.zst` "
"file which can be passed to `heaptrack_gui` for viewing."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:137
msgid "Perf recording"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:139
msgid ""
"How to get a flamegraph with resolved symbols from a running Zed instance. "
"Use this when Zed is using a lot of CPU. It is not useful for hangs."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:142
msgid "During the incident"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:144
msgid ""
"Find the PID (process ID) using: `ps -eo size,pid,comm | grep zed | sort | "
"head -n 1 | cut -d ' ' -f 2` Or find the PID of `zed-editor` with the "
"highest RAM usage in something like htop/btop/top."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:149
msgid ""
"Install perf: On Ubuntu (derivatives) run `sudo apt install linux-tools`."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:152
msgid ""
"Perf record: Run `sudo perf record -p <pid you just found>`, wait a few "
"seconds to gather data, then press Ctrl+C. You should now have a `perf.data` "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:155
msgid "Make the output file user owned: run `sudo chown $USER:$USER perf.data`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:158
msgid ""
"Get build info: Run zed again and type `zed: about` in the command pallet to "
"get the exact commit."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:161
msgid "The `perf.data` file can be sent to Zed together with the exact commit."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:163
msgid "Later"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:165
msgid "This can be done by Zed staff."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:167
msgid ""
"Build Zed with symbols: Check out the commit found previously and modify "
"`Cargo.toml`. Apply the following diff, then make a release build."
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:177
msgid ""
"Add the symbols to the perf database: `perf buildid-cache -v -a <path to "
"release zed binary>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:180
msgid ""
"Resolve the symbols from the db: `perf inject -i perf.data -o "
"perf_with_symbols.data`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:183
msgid "Install flamegraph: `cargo install cargo-flamegraph`"
msgstr ""

#: src/development/linux.md:186
msgid "Render the flamegraph: `flamegraph --perfdata perf_with_symbols.data`"
msgstr ""

